Rem ===================================================================
Rem cave-core.shoddy -- the pure model of Colossal Cave.
Rem
Rem Nothing here prints or reads: no Print, no Input. Every rule of the
Rem cave lives in this file so that test.shoddy can drive it headless,
Rem and cave.shoddy adds the prompts and the transcript on top.
Rem
Rem Ported from open-adventure (Eric S. Raymond, BSD-2-Clause), itself a
Rem forward-port of Crowther & Woods Adventure 2.5. Section comments
Rem carry the C file and line the rule came from, so the two can be
Rem diffed by hand.
Rem ===================================================================

Include "str.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"
Include "cave-messages.shoddy"
Include "cave-locations.shoddy"
Include "cave-travel.shoddy"
Include "cave-objects.shoddy"
Include "cave-vocab.shoddy"
Include "cave-tables.shoddy"

Rem ---- the random number generator -----------------------------------
Rem advent.h:15-19, misc.c:750-777.
Rem
Rem Adventure has carried the same linear congruential generator since
Rem the 1970s: x' = (1093x + 221587) mod 2^20. It matters far more than
Rem it looks. Ninety-two of the hundred-odd recorded test transcripts
Rem pin the stream with an in-band "seed" command, so the whole corpus is
Rem only usable as an oracle if this reproduces bit for bit.
Rem
Rem It does, and the reason is worth writing down: the largest value the
Rem recurrence ever forms is 1093 * 1048575, about 1.15e9, and randrange
Rem never multiplies by more than 1000. Both stay far below 2^53, where
Rem Shoddy's Numbers are still exact integers. So this is not an
Rem approximation of the C -- it is the same arithmetic.

Def LcgA() As Number
    1093

Def LcgC() As Number
    221587

Def LcgM() As Number
    1048576

Rem The C returns the value BEFORE stepping (misc.c:764-772), so a draw
Rem is always "read x, then advance". Keeping those two halves separate
Rem is what lets the caller thread the state purely.

Def LcgNext(x As Number) As Number
    (LcgA() * x + LcgC()) Mod LcgM()

Rem randrange(n) = n * x / 2^20 in truncating integer arithmetic
Rem (misc.c:774-777). Floor is exact here because the product is exact.

Def RandRange(x As Number, n As Number) As Number
    Floor(n * x / LcgM())

Rem PCT(n) is randrange(100) < n -- advent.h:126.

Def Pct(x As Number, n As Number) As Boolean
    RandRange(x, 100) < n

Rem ---- seeding --------------------------------------------------------
Rem misc.c:750-762. set_seed reduces the seed mod 2^20, corrects a
Rem negative, and then consumes exactly five randrange(26) draws to build
Rem the magic word before returning. Those five draws are part of the
Rem stream: skip them and every seeded transcript diverges immediately.
Rem The second character is then overwritten with an apostrophe.

Def SeedX(seed As Number) As Number
    Let r = seed Mod LcgM()
    If r < 0 Then
        r + LcgM()
    Else
        r

Rem Returns the LCG state left behind after the five zzword draws.

Def SeedAdvance(x As Number, n As Number) As Number
    If n = 0 Then
        x
    Else
        SeedAdvance(LcgNext(x), n - 1)

Def SeedState(seed As Number) As Number
    SeedAdvance(SeedX(seed), 5)

Rem The magic word itself: five letters drawn from the stream, with the
Rem second forced to an apostrophe. Adventure calls it the zzword.

Def ZzLetters(x As Number, n As Number, acc As String) As String
    If n = 0 Then
        acc
    Else
        ZzLetters(LcgNext(x), n - 1, acc & Chr(65 + RandRange(x, 26)))

Def ZzWord(seed As Number) As String
    Let w = ZzLetters(SeedX(seed), 5, "")
    Left(w, 1) & "'" & Mid(w, 3, 3)

Rem ---- small helpers ---------------------------------------------------
Rem Written against Nth rather than First/Rest: a Shoddy list is an array
Rem and Rest copies it, so structural recursion over one is quadratic.

Def IndexIn(xs As List, i As Number, n As Number, want As String) As Number
    If i > n Then
        0
    Else
        If Nth(xs, i) = want Then
            i
        Else
            IndexIn(xs, i + 1, n, want)

Rem ---- the parser -----------------------------------------------------
Rem misc.c:380-599. Adventure's grammar is two words and no more, and a
Rem word is significant to its first five letters -- which is why the
Rem game tells you to type "ne" rather than "northeast". The vocabulary
Rem in cave-vocab.shoddy is already stored truncated, so matching is a
Rem plain comparison once both sides are folded.

Def TokLen() As Number
    5

Def Norm(w As String) As String
    Lower(Left(Trim(w), TokLen()))

Rem Word kinds, in the order misc.c:454-505 tries them. The order is not
Rem cosmetic: a word that is both a motion and an object resolves as a
Rem motion, and that shadowing is part of the game's behaviour.
Type Kind = KMotion(Id) | KObject(Id) | KAction(Id) | KMagic | KNumeric(N) | KUnknown

Rem Does this vocabulary entry list the word among its synonyms?
Def HasWord(ws As List, w As String) As Boolean
    If IsEmpty(ws) Then
        False
    Else
        Contains(ws, w)

Def ScanVocab(vs As List, i As Number, n As Number, w As String) As Number
    If i > n Then
        0 - 1
    Else
        If HasWord(Words(Nth(vs, i)), w) Then
            i - 1
        Else
            ScanVocab(vs, i + 1, n, w)

Def ScanObjects(os As List, i As Number, n As Number, w As String) As Number
    If i > n Then
        0 - 1
    Else
        If HasWord(Words(Nth(os, i)), w) Then
            i - 1
        Else
            ScanObjects(os, i + 1, n, w)

Def MotionOf(w As String) As Number
    ScanVocab(Motions(), 1, Length(Motions()), w)

Def ObjectOf(w As String) As Number
    ScanObjects(Objects(), 1, Length(Objects()), w)

Def ActionOf(w As String) As Number
    ScanVocab(Actions(), 1, Length(Actions()), w)

Rem A whole-string digit test; Val aborts on anything else, so nothing
Rem may reach it unguarded.
Def AllDigits(s As String, i As Number, n As Number) As Boolean
    If i > n Then
        True
    Else
        Let c = Mid(s, i, 1)
        If c >= "0" And c <= "9" Then
            AllDigits(s, i + 1, n)
        Else
            False

Def IsInteger(s As String) As Boolean
    If Len(s) = 0 Then
        False
    Else
        If Left(s, 1) = "-" Then
            If Len(s) = 1 Then
                False
            Else
                AllDigits(s, 2, Len(s))
        Else
            AllDigits(s, 1, Len(s))

Rem misc.c:454-505. The magic word is per-game state, drawn from the seed,
Rem so the tokenizer has to be told what it is this time round.
Rem misc.c:386-388 and 417-419. In oldstyle the one-letter abbreviations
Rem of words marked `oldstyle: false` are not words at all -- l, x, g, z
Rem and i were added long after 1977, so the emulation refuses them. The
Rem test only guards motions and actions; objects keep their short forms.
Def Ignored(w As String, old As Boolean) As Boolean
    (old And Len(w) = 1 And Instr(IgnoreSet(), Upper(w)) > 0)

Def Classify(raw As String, magic As String) As Kind
    ClassifyOld(raw, magic, False)

Def ClassifyOld(raw As String, magic As String, old As Boolean) As Kind
    Let w = Norm(raw)
    If Len(w) = 0 Then
        KUnknown()
    Else
        Let m = MotionOf(w)
        If m >= 0 And Not Ignored(w, old) Then
            KMotion(m)
        Else
            Let o = ObjectOf(w)
            If o >= 0 Then
                KObject(o)
            Else
                Let a = ActionOf(w)
                Rem The reservoir word's vocab entry is the placeholder
                Rem z'zzz; the C overwrites it with the seeded word at
                Rem startup, so typing the literal placeholder is unknown.
                If a >= 0 And Not Ignored(w, old) And w <> "z'zzz" Then
                    KAction(a)
                Else
                    If Lower(Trim(raw)) = Lower(magic) Then
                        KMagic()
                    Else
                        If IsInteger(Trim(raw)) Then
                            KNumeric(Val(Trim(raw)))
                        Else
                            KUnknown()

Rem misc.c:507-555. Two words, whitespace separated; anything beyond the
Rem second is refused by word_count before we get here.
Def Tokens(line As String) As List
    Filter(Map(Split(Trim(line), " "), Fn(w) => Trim(w)), Fn(w) => Len(w) > 0)

Def WordAt(ts As List, i As Number) As String
    If Length(ts) < i Then
        ""
    Else
        Nth(ts, i)

Rem misc.c:539-545. Oldstyle mangles the raw token the way packing it into
Rem sixbit characters, five to a 32-bit word, once did: upper-cased and cut
Rem to ten. Not authorial intent -- a limitation of archaic FORTRAN that
Rem Don Wood's translation carried forward -- but the emulation keeps it,
Rem which is why oldstyle scolds you about the word "I" and not "i".
Def RawAt(ts As List, i As Number, old As Boolean) As String
    Let w = WordAt(ts, i)
    If old Then
        Upper(Left(w, 10))
    Else
        w

Rem make_dungeon.py:301-305 and 336-340 build this by walking motions then
Rem actions and collecting the one-letter synonyms of every entry marked
Rem `oldstyle: false`, uppercased. Derived here rather than generated,
Rem since the Oldstyle flag already rides along in the vocabulary tables.
Def IgnoreSet() As String
    IgnoreFrom(Actions(), 1, Length(Actions()),
               IgnoreFrom(Motions(), 1, Length(Motions()), ""))

Def IgnoreFrom(vs As List, i As Number, n As Number, acc As String) As String
    If i > n Then
        acc
    Else
        Let v = Nth(vs, i)
        If Oldstyle(v) Then
            IgnoreFrom(vs, i + 1, n, acc)
        Else
            IgnoreFrom(vs, i + 1, n, Singles(Words(v), 1, Length(Words(v)), acc))

Def Singles(ws As List, i As Number, n As Number, acc As String) As String
    If i > n Then
        acc
    Else
        If Len(Nth(ws, i)) = 1 Then
            Singles(ws, i + 1, n, acc & Upper(Nth(ws, i)))
        Else
            Singles(ws, i + 1, n, acc)
